-- erwartet: Hinweis E009

-- **A real lock-order inversion behind an incomplete hull passes -- race form 7, R16.**
--
-- `ping` holds `L2` (rank 2) and calls `pong`; `pong` takes `L1` (rank 1) and calls
-- back. At runtime that is an ABBA deadlock whenever the counter is positive: each
-- side holds one lock and waits for the other through the call. The checker reports
-- nothing but the honest third state. The ping/pong cycle cuts both effect hulls, so
-- `H012` (`Rufwissen::nimmt`, `geteilt.rs`) sees an incomplete hull and stays silent
-- (R16), and `H006` sees no nested `locks` block in either body.
--
-- The control is `gift/142`: the same call shape without a cycle falls with `H012`.
-- The `decreases` measures are honest termination bookkeeping (K008/K009 stay silent
-- because of them, not in spite of them); they change nothing about the lock order.
--
-- Refusing over the visible lower bound instead would invert R16, and it is not
-- provably safe: the visible hull over a cycle is built from DECLARED effects, and
-- `messung/proben/460` measures that declared `locks` over-states who takes what (a
-- correct program refused). A lower-bound refusal would refuse correct programs of
-- the 460 shape wherever a cycle passes nearby. So the silence stands documented
-- here, not built. (`sperren.rangordnung` in the pass register and section 5(a)
-- of `messung/H006.md` book the same boundary.)
module gift::rangumkehr_hinter_zyklus {

const TIEFE : u32 = 16;

static mut a : u32 = 0;
static mut b : u32 = 0;
lock L1 protects { a } rank 1 held <= 100 ops;
lock L2 protects { b } rank 2 held <= 100 ops;

impl fn ping(t : u32 in 0 .. TIEFE)
    effects { writes a, writes b, locks L1, locks L2 }
    costs   <= 64 ops
    decreases t
{
    locks L2 {
        b = 2;
        if t >= 1 {
            pong(t - 1);
        }
    }
}

impl fn pong(t : u32 in 0 .. TIEFE)
    effects { writes a, writes b, locks L1, locks L2 }
    costs   <= 64 ops
    decreases t
{
    locks L1 {
        a = 2;
        if t >= 1 {
            ping(t - 1);
        }
    }
}

}
